That rather trivializes the evidence of the senses, doesn't it?

Perry wrote:
> Sorry, Mark, but "buses you do not see do not exist" follows directly
> from "sensory evidence is valid".

Sell my shares if I'm belaboring the obvious, but my sensory evidence
about busses in Chicago is valid -- it's just that I haven't got any.
I can't see a bus from the vat where I'm sitting to write this, but
I can't see no-bus either.

Dave wrote:
